!! shows ~ a-patch · a-new-record · an-append · a-span · a-whole-carrier · a-slot · a-cut

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-patch` params=`title/[[Room 4]] recipe/default fields/{"todo":"done"} tag-add/reviewed base/<hash> ~ a field and tag patch; the text stays`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-new-record` params=`title/[[New Note]] recipe/default create/true text/[[first words]] ~ lands only where no record stands`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`an-append` params=`title/Ledger recipe/default append/note.txt ~ the words land at the end with no base; two appends at once both land`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-span` params=`title/[[Room 4]] recipe/default replace/[[by the window]] with/[[by the door]] base/<hash> ~ one exact span changes; zero or two occurrences refuse`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-whole-carrier` params=`title/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/x recipe/lares file/x.mem ~ a whole carrier lands the family; an omitted slot stays, named under kept`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-slot` params=`title/lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/x recipe/default slot/#/why text/[[the reason, rewritten]] ~ one slot's text, no base; the family reseals`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-cut` params=`title/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/x recipe/lares file/x.mem cut-slot/#/old ~ the carrier lands and #/old leaves by name`>>
```

